  "solution": {
    "text": "Given:&nbsp;Heat of combustion of carbon and carbon monoxide are <math><mo>-</mo><mn>393.5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>283.5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> respectively.<br /><br />(i) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>393.5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />(ii) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>283.5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />To find the heat of formation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CO</mi></math> per mole.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#916;</mo> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mtext>f</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </mrow> </math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CO</mi></math><br /><br />From equations (i) and (ii),<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>=-393.5-</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>283</mn><mo>.5</mo></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>"
